{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Errors</b> — It is possible that the alef stands in place of a doubled letter or in place of yod, like 'שכיות חמדה' (desirable vessels?). And the meaning: I am careful with all my might; only I fear lest perhaps an error befall me. Therefore he said: 'From hidden faults, clear me.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The phrase שכיות חמדה is opaque; rendered hyper-literally as 'desirable vessels,' following its occurrence in Isaiah 32:12 or as a lexical illustration of alef replacing a doubled letter or yod. The precise grammatical point Ibn Ezra is making about the alef in שגיאות is textually uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:55.244338818Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}